          "skill": "Main Purpose",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Analyze the primary purpose or rhetorical intent of the text as a whole",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 8 · Q19",
          "passageTitle": "Main Purpose — Q19",
          "passage": "San Francisco has high pedestrian traffic, but\nsimply replicating a feature of San Francisco\nassociated with walkability—e.g. its high\ndensity of storefronts—may be insufficient to\ninduce increased walking in other cities. As\nurbanist Mariela Alfonzo argues, our\nunderstanding of individuals decision-making\nabout whether to walk is insufficiently robust:\nsome studies emphasize the role of demographic\ncharacteristics, others the role of public transit\navailability, and so on, but walking decisions are\nmade in complex contexts in which multiple\nconditions and needs inform individuals' choices.",
