          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 8 · Q34",
          "passageTitle": "Main Purpose — Q34",
          "passage": "The following text is from Bram Stoker's 1911\nnovel The Lair of the White Worm. Adam is\nmeeting his great-uncle Richard at a port.\nThe meeting so auspiciously begun proceeded\nwell. Adam, seeing that the old man was\ninterested in the novelty of the ship, suggested\nthat he should stay the night on board, and that\nhe would himself be ready to start at any hour\nand go anywhere that the other suggested. This\naffectionate willingness to fall in with his own\nplans quite won the old man's heart. He warmly\naccepted the invitation, and at once they\nbecame not only on terms of affectionate\nrelationship, but almost like old friends.",
